    [Ops][BugFix] Enable A5 MegaMoE for Qwen4Exp with 2560 hidden size and preserve routing for unquantized MTP drafts (#20502)
    
    ## Summary
    
    Backport the behavior of #20402 onto `releases/v0.32.0rc` (base
    `ffca1c99b`).
    
    - Allow hidden size 2560 for the A5 MegaMoE Qwen3.8 Flash Next
    configuration.
    - Keep quantized target MoE layers on MegaMoE. When an unquantized MoE
    layer is reached while the V2 context selected MegaMoE, select that
    layer's communication method using the existing A5 capacity/world-size
    policy and keep the context type in sync.
    - Limit the draft's ordinary MC2 capacity to 512 tokens per TP rank when
    MegaMoE's larger shared capacity was selected.
    - For an unsupported-quantized MTP draft with sequence parallel MoE
    enabled, skip ordinary MC2 as well. On EP4/top-k10 this selects
    AllGather at every draft token count; without SP, the existing MC2
    capacity policy remains in effect. The quantized target continues to use
    FUSED_MC2, and the MegaMoE-disabled route is unchanged.
    
    The PR contains the #20402 code path and tests adapted to the release
    branch. It does not include #20311 or the separate PLE INT8 runtime
    adaptation.
    
    ## Validation
    
    - Exact PR head `33d316210` in an isolated Ascend container worktree:
    `python -m pytest -q tests/ut/test_ascend_forward_context.py` — 59
    passed. The SP regression covers 1, 1024, and 4096 tokens for the
    unquantized draft, and verifies that the target remains on FUSED_MC2.
    - Earlier release-branch validation: 87 targeted unit cases passed (A5
    config, draft capacity, per-layer route, MegaMoE-disabled path).
    - Changed files: `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, and `git diff
    --check` passed.
    - `bash format.sh ci` was attempted in the Ascend container but could
    not initialize `ruff-pre-commit`: the configured proxy refused the
    GitHub connection. The focused Ruff checks above passed.
    - The combined development runtime on 8 A5 NPUs reproduced
    `MoeDistributeDispatchV3 Get WinSize failed` before the SP route fix.
    After applying this route fix, P/D proxy smoke requests completed
    (32/32), and two full GPQA Diamond runs completed (198/198 requests
    each; 88.89% and 91.92% accuracy with `temperature=1.0`). This runtime
    also contains #20311 and PLE INT8 changes, so this is integration
    evidence, not a standalone E2E test of this release PR.
    
    ## Integration status
    
    The SP draft communication fix is included in this PR. Direct E2E
    validation of the exact `releases/v0.32.0rc` PR stack remains pending;
    the 8-card P/D run used the combined development runtime. The PR remains
    draft.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
